## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/rasterizegeo.html
- Summary (EN): Rasterize Geometry rasterizes polygon geometry onto a layer and can also rasterize geometry attributes such as alpha, position, normals, UVs and depth. The page does not show its file name; the Copernicus node index lists Rasterize Geometry as rasterizegeo.html, so the identity is strong but inferred.
- Résumé (FR) : Ce nœud rastérise de la géométrie polygonale sur un calque et peut transporter ses attributs, comme l'alpha, les normales ou les UV.

- Inputs meaning: ["camera_ref: optional camera metadata, typically from a Camera Import node; without it the node uses the COPnet resolution, sits at the origin and looks down the negative Z axis", "geometry: polygon geometry to rasterize, usually from a SOP Import COP"]

- Key parameters: ["Quick Setups: one-click Alpha, Position, Normal, UV or Depth from Eye attributes, or move output layers to canonical space", "Border: sampling outside the layer boundaries, defaults to the layer border property", "Depth Mode: rasterize data from the minimum or maximum depth sample", "Face Culling: No Culling, Backface or Frontface", "Number of Attributes: Output Type, Name (special tokens intrinsic:alpha, intrinsic:depth_ndc and intrinsic:depth_eye generate layers), Optional flag falling back to a layer defined by size_ref, and Default Value"]

- Caveats: ["The geometry must be polygons. Packed geometry and volumes are not supported.", "Attributes must be an integer, or a float with 4 or fewer components, to be rasterized.", "The Normal and UV quick setups require those attributes to exist on the input geometry.", "With camera_ref connected, the layer is generated at the camera focus plane; the page suggests Match Camera to move it back to the origin.", "The Optional fallback refers to a size_ref input that the page does not list among the node's inputs.", "The Rasterize Setup COP can change the space in which rasterization happens, such as UV space."]

